-- check/good: a `case` of 1 200 branches `[ Just ( k, y ), …rest ]` plus a
-- wildcard — ordinary code, generated (see tests/corpus/README.md).
--
-- A `case` like this must not be REFUSED at the default budget. Judging
-- every branch against the branches above it specialised afresh read every
-- row above it three times before the literal `k` dropped it, ~4·n² steps:
-- 1 200 branches came to more than the default 5 000 000, and this was
-- `pattern_budget_exhausted` on a `case` with nothing wrong with it (issue
-- #812). Usefulness walks a tree of the specialised matrices, kept for the
-- whole `case` (`checker-v2.md` §16, amended 2026-10-23), so this costs 23
-- steps a branch. The number of branches is chosen to cross the old
-- threshold, so this fixture fails the moment a branch reads the rows above
-- it again.
pub f : List (Maybe (Int × Int)) → Int
f xs =
    case xs of
        [ Just ( 0, y ), …rest ] →
            y

        [ Just ( 1, y ), …rest ] →
            y

        [ Just ( 2, y ), …rest ] →
            y

